<title>USA: Allegiant agrees to buy two bank offices.</title>
<headline>Allegiant agrees to buy two bank offices.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allegiant Bancorp Inc said it has signed an agreement to purchase the Roosevelt Bank offices in Warrenton and Union, Missouri.</p>
<p>Terms of the transaction were not disclosed.</p>
<p>In a release dated May 8, Allegiant said the purchase, which is subject to regulatory approvals, includes branch buildings, as well as safe deposit, loan and deposit relationships.</p>
<p>After completion of the deal, Allegiant will operate 14 locations with total assets of more than $500 million.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
